; expect 42
; Field access by name on a `data` type stays legal when every
; constructor declares the field at the same word with the same
; type: the emitter loads one index for the name, and here every
; constructor agrees on it. The partial shapes - a constructor that
; does not declare the field, or declares it elsewhere - are refused
; as AX3070 (tests/diagnostics/484-field-on-partial-data.ax).
(data Shape
  (Circle { r : Int })
  (Dot { r : Int }))

(:: radius (-> Shape Int))
(fn (radius s) s.r)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (radius (Dot 42)))
